`schema.filter` is used here both as a query filter (passed to `$filter`) and as the container for calendar view config (`filter.calendar`). Passing the whole object to `$filter` will likely produce invalid queries. Only send `$filter` when it’s actually a filter expression/array, and keep view config in a separate field.
```suggestion

          const filterConfig = (schema as any).filter;
          const hasCalendarConfig =
            filterConfig &&
            typeof filterConfig === 'object' &&
            !Array.isArray(filterConfig) &&
            'calendar' in filterConfig;
          const queryFilter =
            typeof filterConfig === 'string' || Array.isArray(filterConfig) || (filterConfig && !hasCalendarConfig)
              ? filterConfig
              : undefined;

          const result = await dataSource.find(objectName, {
            ...(queryFilter !== undefined ? { $filter: queryFilter } : {}),
```

`schema.filter` is being passed directly to `dataSource.find` as `$filter`, but in these view schemas `schema.filter` is also being used to store the view config (e.g., `filter.kanban`). That will send non-filter config objects to the backend and likely break queries. Consider separating view config from query filters (or only pass `$filter` when `schema.filter` is an actual filter array).
```suggestion
          const queryFilter = Array.isArray(schema.filter) ? schema.filter : undefined;
          const result = await dataSource.find(objectName, {
            $filter: queryFilter,
```

`uniqueValues` is built with `.filter(Boolean)`, which will drop legitimate falsy group values (e.g., `0`, `false`, or empty string). This can cause records to disappear from the board. Filter only `null`/`undefined` (or use a dedicated predicate) instead.
```suggestion
    // Get unique values for grouping field (exclude only null/undefined)
    const uniqueValues = [...new Set(data.map(record => record[groupByField]))].filter(
      (value) => value != null
    );
```

`$filter: schema.filter` will include the gantt view config (`filter.gantt`) in addition to any real query filters, which is likely not a valid backend filter format. Consider splitting query filters from view configuration, or conditionally passing `$filter` only when the schema provides an actual filter expression/array.
```suggestion
          const queryOptions: any = {
            $orderby: convertSortToQueryParams(schema.sort),
          };

          // Only pass $filter when schema.filter is a backend-valid filter expression/array,
          // to avoid leaking view-specific config (e.g. filter.gantt) into the query.
          if (schema.filter && (Array.isArray(schema.filter) || typeof schema.filter === 'string')) {
            queryOptions.$filter = schema.filter;
          }

          const result = await dataSource.find(objectName, queryOptions);
```
